  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $4.8B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury made 6,923 awards with an average award size of $696K. Obligations are down 43.6% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a peak at $10.3B in FY23 and declines to $8.5B in FY25 before reaching $4.8B in FY26. The Top 10 categories in FY2026 to date are led by Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $1B and Other Computer Related Services at $937M. The Department of the Treasury’s vendor list in FY2026 to date is led by STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $885M, followed by ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $384M and FCN, INC. at $197M. The distribution of obligations shows both metals and computer services among the largest categories, and a mix of large specialized suppliers and federal services firms among the top vendors. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does Treasury's FY2026 to date spending compare to recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $4.8B in FY2026 to date, down 43.6% year over year. Obligations were $8.5B in FY25, $9.3B in FY24, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY22, and $9.6B in FY21. The year-over-year decline to $4.8B is the largest single-year drop shown in the fiscal sequence. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate Treasury contracting in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining is the largest NAICS category at $1B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $937M and Computer Systems Design Services at $448M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is the largest vendor at $885M, followed by ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $384M and FCN, INC. at $197M. The Top 10 categories mix metals, computer services, and logistics, and the Top 10 vendors mix refiners, financial services, and federal services firms."
      }
    ]
  },
