    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Treasury spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $4.8B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury recorded 6,923 awards with an average award size of $696K. Obligations are down 43.6% year over year and prior-year totals include $8.5B in FY25 and $10.3B in FY23."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Treasury buy?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury buys a mix of metals, computer services, manufacturing, and logistics in FY2026 to date. Top NAICS categories include Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $1B, Other Computer Related Services at $937M, Computer Systems Design Services at $448M, and General Warehousing and Storage at $95.3M."
